@startuml Weaver Integration Detailed Sequence

!define CRITICAL #FF6B6B
!define SUCCESS #2ECC71
!define PROCESSING #3498DB

title Detailed Weaver Integration Sequence (End-to-End)

actor "Developer" as Dev
participant "clnrm CLI" as CLI
participant "WeawerController" as Controller
participant "TestEngine" as Engine
participant "Generated\nTelemetry" as GenTelemetry
participant "Container\nManager" as ContainerMgr
participant "Docker" as Docker
participant "OTLP\nExporter" as OTLP
participant "Weaver\nLive-Check" as Weaver
database "Telemetry\nRegistry" as Registry

== Initialization Phase ==

Dev -> CLI : clnrm run tests/ --validate-telemetry
activate CLI #PROCESSING

CLI -> Controller : initialize with validation
activate Controller #PROCESSING

Controller -> Registry : load telemetry schemas
activate Registry
Registry --> Controller : schemas loaded
note right
  Loaded schemas:
  - test_execution
  - container_lifecycle
  - plugin_system
  - test_metrics
end note

Controller -> Weaver : start live-check listener
activate Weaver #CRITICAL
note right of Weaver
  weaver registry live-check \
    --registry registry/ \
    --otlp-grpc-port 4317 \
    --output ./validation/ \
    --format json
end note
Weaver --> Controller : listener started on :4317

Controller -> OTLP : configure exporter
activate OTLP
OTLP --> Controller : exporter ready

Controller --> CLI : validation environment ready
deactivate Registry

== Test Execution Phase ==

CLI -> Engine : execute test suite
activate Engine #PROCESSING

loop For each test in TOML

  Engine -> GenTelemetry : create_test_execution_span()
  activate GenTelemetry
  note right
    Generated from schema:

    TestExecutionSpan::new(
      test_name,
      container_image
    )
  end note
  GenTelemetry --> Engine : span created

  Engine -> ContainerMgr : create_isolated_container()
  activate ContainerMgr

  ContainerMgr -> GenTelemetry : create_container_lifecycle_span()
  GenTelemetry --> ContainerMgr : span created

  ContainerMgr -> Docker : docker run alpine:latest
  activate Docker
  Docker --> ContainerMgr : container_id: "abc123"

  ContainerMgr -> GenTelemetry : span.set_container_id("abc123")
  ContainerMgr -> GenTelemetry : span.set_state(ContainerState::Running)

  note right of GenTelemetry #SUCCESS
    Telemetry automatically includes:
    - container.id = "abc123"
    - container.image = "alpine:latest"
    - container.state = "running"
    - test.isolated = true

    ALL required by schema
  end note

  ContainerMgr --> Engine : container ready

  Engine -> Docker : execute test commands
  Docker --> Engine : command results

  Engine -> GenTelemetry : span.set_test_result(TestResult::Pass)
  Engine -> GenTelemetry : span.record_duration(125.5)

  deactivate Docker

  ' Export telemetry
  Engine -> OTLP : export_span(test_execution_span)
  OTLP -> Weaver : stream telemetry via OTLP gRPC
  note right of OTLP
    OTLP Span Export:
    {
      "name": "test_execution",
      "attributes": {
        "container.id": "abc123",
        "container.image": "alpine:latest",
        "test.isolated": true,
        "test.result": "pass",
        "duration_ms": 125.5
      }
    }
  end note

  ' Real-time validation
  Weaver -> Registry : load schema for validation
  activate Registry
  Weaver -> Weaver : validate span against schema
  deactivate Registry

  alt Span Matches Schema
    Weaver -> Weaver : log: ✓ validation passed
    note right of Weaver #SUCCESS
      Validation PASSED:
      ✓ container.id present (required)
      ✓ test.isolated = true (required)
      ✓ test.result valid enum (required)
      ✓ All types match schema

      TRUE POSITIVE
      Feature is working!
    end note
  else Span Doesn't Match Schema
    Weaver -> Weaver : log: ✗ violation found
    note right of Weaver #CRITICAL
      Validation FAILED:
      ✗ Missing required attribute:
        container.id

      FALSE NEGATIVE
      Container may not have run!
      Test result invalid!
    end note
  end

  ' Cleanup
  ContainerMgr -> Docker : docker rm abc123
  Docker --> ContainerMgr : removed
  deactivate ContainerMgr

  ContainerMgr -> GenTelemetry : span.end()
  GenTelemetry -> OTLP : export_span(container_lifecycle_span)
  OTLP -> Weaver : stream lifecycle telemetry

  deactivate GenTelemetry

end

Engine --> CLI : all tests completed
deactivate Engine

== Validation Report Phase ==

CLI -> Controller : request validation results
Controller -> Weaver : stop listener & generate report
deactivate OTLP

Weaver -> Weaver : aggregate all validations
Weaver -> Weaver : calculate statistics

note right of Weaver
  Statistics:
  - total_entities: 15
  - total_advisories: 16
  - violation: 2
  - improvement: 3
  - information: 11
  - registry_coverage: 85%
end note

Weaver --> Controller : validation report
deactivate Weaver

Controller -> Controller : parse validation results

alt All Validations Passed
  Controller --> CLI : ValidationResult::Success #SUCCESS
  note right
    {
      "status": "success",
      "violations": 0,
      "coverage": 0.85,
      "total_tests": 15,
      "message": "All telemetry validated"
    }
  end note

  CLI --> Dev : ✓ Tests passed\n✓ Telemetry validated\nExit code: 0 #SUCCESS

  note over Dev #SUCCESS
    **SAFE TO SHIP**

    Tests passed ✓
    Weaver validation passed ✓

    Features proven to work!
  end note

else Any Validation Failed
  Controller --> CLI : ValidationResult::Failure #CRITICAL
  note right
    {
      "status": "failure",
      "violations": 2,
      "details": [
        {
          "test": "http_test",
          "issue": "missing container.id",
          "level": "violation"
        }
      ]
    }
  end note

  CLI --> Dev : ✗ Tests passed\n✗ Telemetry validation FAILED\nExit code: 1 #CRITICAL

  note over Dev #CRITICAL
    **DO NOT SHIP**

    Tests passed ✓
    Weaver validation FAILED ✗

    Feature may have false positives!
    Fix implementation or schema.
  end note
end

deactivate Controller
deactivate CLI

== The Critical Decision Point ==

note over Dev, Registry #FFEB9C
  **THE WEAVER DECISION GATE**

  Traditional Approach:
    Tests pass → Ship it
    └─ Risk: False positives

  clnrm Approach:
    Tests pass AND Weaver validates → Ship it
    └─ Proof: Runtime behavior proven

  **If Weaver validation fails:**
  1. Implementation bug (fix code)
  2. Schema incorrect (fix schema)
  3. Configuration issue (fix config)
  4. Test not exercising code (fix test)

  **Never ship without Weaver validation passing.**

  This is the ONLY way to prove features work.
end note

@enduml
